# Generated Documentation

Files in this directory are reproducible facts generated from source, schemas, tests, or tooling.

Every generated file must identify its generator near the top. Do not edit generated output manually. Change the source or generator, regenerate, and verify drift in CI.

- `repository-facts.md` separates directly observed paths from mechanically derived language, runtime, and command candidates. Every row names an evidence path; neither class is normative authority.
- `baseline-questions.md` names authority questions that observation cannot answer. Resolve them in project-owned drafts or an active plan rather than editing generated output.
- `code-map.md` derives evidence-backed path routing for the repository-local context command.
